# A fake diamond, coated: cubic zirconia (glass:cubic-zirconia, n_d 2.15, fire 0.060) under a
# 60 nm film of titania (glass:titania, 2.44 at 550 nm). 60 nm is a quarter wave in the film,
# where its reflections add: the facets reflect 22 % face-on instead of bare CZ's 13 %, with no
# colour -- the brighter surface sparkle such a coating is for. The stone's refraction and fire
# are its own; the film does not change them. Titania and CZ are close in index, so a thicker
# film only tints: pink at 100 and 200 nm, pale cyan at 150. For a coloured "mystic" look use
# glass, where the contrast is larger (preset titania-coating). A clear coating: the stone
# refracts, so give it a closed shape.
# aliases: titania-coated-cz coated-cz
type thinfilm
ior            glass:cubic-zirconia
film_ior       glass:titania
film_thickness 60
